# id: FLOOR-continuation-removed
# blinds: the sweep's detection power, not any engine behaviour
# covering-lane: cpp-campaign
# expect: killed
# control-lane: cpp-sweep
# expect-control: alive
#
# THE HARNESS-POWER REGRESSION, INDUCED. Nothing about the engine changes and
# nothing goes red: the sweep still visits 175 kill points, still reports 175
# passes, still observes both elements of the recovery set. It has simply
# stopped being able to see one class of defect.
#
# BM2 measured 194 per mille with the continuation and ZERO without it, because
# recovery applies uncommitted records ABOVE the recovered watermark, where the
# snapshot hides them until a reopened database resumes service. A drop from 194
# to 0 must break the build rather than appear in a report nobody diffs.
#
# The control is cpp-sweep staying GREEN, and that is the whole demonstration:
# the lane whose job is to find defects is perfectly healthy, and its power has
# collapsed. That is the exact shape Track A lost five checklist steps to.
#
# REGENERATED AT B2.7. The continuation grew a Sync, a filler batch and a SECOND
# RECOVERY while CF-1's predicted second detection path was being hunted, so the
# patch is re-cut against the whole block. What it blinds is unchanged: remove
# the continuation and BM2 goes from 34 detections to zero while every lane stays
# green.
